# Unity Project Guidelines

## Code Style & Formatting
- Language: C# (Unity 2022.3+ compatible)
- Naming Conventions: Use PascalCase for methods/classes, camelCase for local variables/private fields.
- Access Modifiers: Always explicitly state 'private', 'protected', or 'public'.
- Architecture Style: Use MonoBehavior Singletons for global managers. Use ScriptableObjects for data-driven systems.

## Unity Specifics
- Always use cached component references (do not call GetComponent inside Update).
- Use Vector3.MoveTowards or Lerp with Time.deltaTime for smooth movement.
- Keep UI separate from gameplay logic using event-driven communication (Actions/UnityEvents).
